# CLAUDE.md — app/ (backend code design)

Scope: `app/`: **how to write the code**. Each layer directory's `CLAUDE.md` elaborates it; read it before writing
there.

## Layout — flat by layer, no modules

One domain, so no modules. If that changes, record the decision after `house:end` below; never an ad-hoc
`app/Modules/`.

```
app/
├── Actions/Fortify/    # Fortify's auth actions (CreateNewUser, ResetUserPassword, …)
├── Console/Commands/   # artisan commands (scheduler entry points, ops)
├── Contracts/          # interfaces — the seams to outside systems
├── Enums/              # domain vocabulary + lifecycle state machines
├── Events/             # domain events
├── Http/
│   ├── Controllers/    # thin HTTP translation
│   └── Middleware/     # request-scoped cross-cutting only
├── Jobs/               # queued work
├── Listeners/
├── Models/
├── Policies/
├── Providers/
├── Requests/           # FormRequests — one per endpoint
├── Resources/          # API Resources — one per exposed entity
├── Services/           # domain services, list queries, external clients
└── Support/            # small, security-relevant helpers only
```

FormRequests live in `app/Requests` and Resources in `app/Resources`, **never** `app/Http/Requests` or
`app/Http/Resources`: a second home would fragment them. `app/Http/` holds framework plumbing only.
<!-- if:htmx -->
<!-- if:islands -->
Everything rendered lives under `resources/` (`resources/CLAUDE.md`): Blade views and anonymous components in
`resources/views/`, Svelte islands in `resources/js/islands/`.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
Everything rendered lives under `resources/` (`resources/CLAUDE.md`): Blade views and anonymous components in
`resources/views/`.
<!-- endif -->
A class-based Blade component goes in `app/View/Components/` only when it needs PHP; create the directory with its
own `CLAUDE.md` then.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:spa -->
Everything rendered lives in the SvelteKit app under `frontend/` (`frontend/CLAUDE.md`); Laravel serves JSON only.
<!-- endif -->

## The layering rule

A controller action is HTTP translation only (`app/Http/Controllers/CLAUDE.md`). These concerns belong below it:

| Concern | Owner — never the controller |
|---------|------------------------------|
| **Transaction boundary** | The service or model that owns the write. A controller opening `DB::transaction` means the workflow wants a service. |
| **Status transition** | The model's `transitionTo()` consulting the enum's `canTransitionTo()`. Never `$m->status = 'done'` or `update(['status' => …])` in an action. |
| **Derived/aggregate computation** | A service or model method. Private controller helpers computing business values are the tell. |
| **Event dispatch** | The layer that performs the state change dispatches its own events. |
| **Export / bulk plumbing** | A shared concern, never a hand-rolled per-controller `export()` pair. |

<!-- if:htmx -->
**The read path stays cheap**, even behind the response cache: eager-load what the view renders, aggregate and
paginate in SQL, `Cache::flexible` anything slow, index every column a public page filters or sorts by. A write to a
publicly rendered entity **invalidates the response-cache tags that show it**, in the model event or domain service
that writes, never in the controller.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:htmx -->
**The read path stays cheap**: eager-load what the Resource renders, aggregate and paginate in SQL,
`Cache::flexible` anything slow, index every column a list endpoint filters or sorts by.
<!-- endif -->

## Models — fat, in the Laravel sense

Models own their own state: casts, relations, scopes, accessors, predicates, guards and state transitions.
Multi-model orchestration goes to a service (`app/Models/CLAUDE.md`).

## Records that must not be rewritten

An audit trail or a record of what happened is **append-only**: a correction is a new row superseding the old one
(`supersedes_id`), never an update or delete. A job observing external state **snapshots absolute state, not
deltas**, stamped when *observed*, not inserted. Which tables get this is recorded in `app/Models/CLAUDE.md`.

## Services — a deliberate taxonomy

**Single-model invariant → model method; multi-model workflow → domain service; external system → a contract-backed
client; reusable filter → ListQuery** (`app/Services/CLAUDE.md`). Every external system sits behind a contract in
`Contracts/`; what an E2E test fakes is `tests/CLAUDE.md`'s.

## Octane: no request state in shared position

Production runs **FrankenPHP + Octane**, so the app stays in memory between requests; the local php-fpm does not.
State discarded per request locally leaks in production, across requests and *users*. Only a warm worker shows it.

- **Never** keep request-specific state in a singleton, a static property or a captured closure variable.
  Per-request services are `$this->app->scoped()`, never `singleton()`; a binding never captures the current request
  or user.
- Reset transient flags in a `finally`, not at the end of the happy path.
- A static cache keyed by "the user currently being handled" is a cross-user leak.
- `config('octane.server')` names the active driver when something must branch.
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- **The tenant is connection state too.** Octane and the queue worker flush the `scoped()` `CurrentTenant`, but not
  `app.tenant_id` on the reused PDO connection. A setting left behind becomes the next request's tenant.
  - Set it at every request start (`ResolveTenant`) and every job start (`Context::hydrated`).
  - Reset it to `''` in `App\Listeners\ResetTenantConnection`, registered in `config/octane.php` under
    `RequestReceived` and `RequestTerminated`.
  - Never reset it in a middleware `terminate()`: deferred callbacks and after-response jobs run after it, and
    Octane skips terminate when sending the response fails.
  - Re-apply it on reconnect (`ConnectionEstablished`).
  - Never set it inside an application `DB::transaction()`: a rollback undoes it.
<!-- endif -->

## Off-request rules (jobs, listeners, commands, services)

Queued and scheduled work has **no authenticated user, no request locale, no request context**.

- Whatever a job scopes by is **passed in explicitly**: the user or entity id comes from the work item, never from
  `auth()` or `request()`.
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- **Exception: the tenant**, carried in hidden Context (`app/Jobs/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- endif -->
- **Idempotent** (delivery is at least once): a re-run upserts on the natural key and repeats no side effect (email,
  charge, API call). `ShouldBeUnique` where a second concurrent copy is wrong.
- Fan out **one job per item** (`Bus::batch()` when the group matters), so one hung item stalls nothing else.
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- A command or scheduled task over tenant data loops over the tenants and dispatches one job per tenant inside
  `CurrentTenant::run($id, …)`.
- Cache keys of tenant data include `t:{tenant_id}:`.
<!-- endif -->
- Queued payloads hold class names: renaming a job, event or listener breaks in-flight payloads. Before such a
  release, stop dispatching it and wait for empty queues (`horizon:status`), or keep a `class_alias`.
  `horizon:pause` holds payloads; it does not remove them.

## User-authored text is untrusted input

Anything a user or external system typed is stored raw and handled the same way everywhere:

<!-- if:htmx -->
- Escape on output, always: Blade `{{ }}`; `{!! !!}` only for `Markdown::render()` (raw HTML escaped). The CSP is the
  second layer.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:spa -->
- Escape on output, always: Svelte `{text}`; `{@html}` only for `Markdown::render()` (raw HTML escaped). The CSP is
  the second layer.
<!-- endif -->
- Validate **size and shape**, never content-filter on write: a write-time filter silently rewrites the data.
- It never reaches a component that can act on it (a shell, an LLM with tools, an eval) without a deliberate decision
  recorded in this file, after `house:end`.
<!-- house:end -->
